{"id":"mahabharata-11-015","work":"mahabharata","part":11,"partName":"स्त्रीपर्व","partNameEn":"Stri Parva","unit":15,"title":"पञ्चदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 15 · Gandhari and Yudhishthira; Draupadi's grief","summary":{"en":"Gandhari, in anger, asks where Yudhishthira is, and he comes with folded hands and offers himself to her curse. She looks at his toes through her blindfold and his nails are burnt, and Kunti comforts the weeping Draupadi.","kn":"ಗಾಂಧಾರಿ ಕೋಪದಿಂದ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಎಲ್ಲಿ ಎಂದು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾಳೆ; ಅವನು ಕೈಮುಗಿದು ಬಂದು ತನ್ನ ಶಾಪಕ್ಕೆ ತನ್ನನ್ನೇ ಅರ್ಪಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕಣ್ಣಿನ ಪಟ್ಟಿಯ ಮೂಲಕ ಅವನ ಕಾಲ್ಬೆರಳು ನೋಡುತ್ತಾಳೆ, ಅವನ ಉಗುರುಗಳು ಸುಟ್ಟಿವೆ; ಅಳುತ್ತಿರುವ ದ್ರೌಪದಿಯನ್ನು ಕುಂತಿ ಸಂತೈಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"गान्धारी क्रोध से पूछती हैं कि युधिष्ठिर कहाँ है, और वे हाथ जोड़कर आकर स्वयं को उनके शाप के लिए अर्पित करते हैं। वे पट्टी के पार उनकी उँगलियाँ देखती हैं और उनके नाखून झुलस जाते हैं, और कुन्ती रोती द्रौपदी को सान्त्वना देती हैं।","te":"గాంధారి కోపంతో యుధిష్ఠిరుడు ఎక్కడని అడుగుతుంది; అతడు చేతులు జోడించి వచ్చి తనను ఆమె శాపానికి అర్పిస్తాడు. కట్టు గుండా అతని కాలివేళ్లను చూస్తుంది, అతని గోళ్లు కాలిపోతాయి; ఏడుస్తున్న ద్రౌపదిని కుంతి ఓదారుస్తుంది.","ta":"காந்தாரி சினத்துடன் யுதிஷ்டிரர் எங்கே என்று கேட்க, அவர் கைகூப்பி வந்து தன்னை அவள் சாபத்துக்கு அளிக்கிறார். கண்கட்டின் வழியே அவர் கால்விரல்களைப் பார்க்க, அவர் நகங்கள் கருகுகின்றன; அழும் திரௌபதியைக் குந்தி தேற்றுகிறாள்.","ml":"കോപത്തോടെ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ എവിടെയെന്ന് ഗാന്ധാരി ചോദിക്കുന്നു; അദ്ദേഹം കൈകൂപ്പി അവളുടെ ശാപത്തിന് സ്വയം സമർപ്പിക്കുന്നു. കണ്ണുകെട്ടിലൂടെ അവൾ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന്റെ കാൽവിരലുകളെ നോക്കുന്നു; നഖങ്ങൾ കരിഞ്ഞുപോകുന്നു. കരയുന്ന ദ്രൗപദിയെ കുന്തി ആശ്വസിപ്പിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 11.15; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 17 2017","sections":[{"title":"जलप्रदानिकपर्व","titleEn":"Jalapradanika Parva (The water offerings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा तु गान्धारी युधिष्ठिरमपृच्छत ।\nक्व स राजेति सक्रोधा पुत्रपौत्रवधार्दिता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having spoken so, Gandhari, in anger and pained by the killing of her sons and grandsons, asked Yudhishthira, \"Where is that king?\""}},{"n":2,"text":"तामभ्यगच्छद्राजेन्द्रो वेपमानः कृताञ्जलिः ।\nयुधिष्ठिर इदं चैनां मधुरं वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Yudhishthira approached her, trembling with joined palms, and said to her these gentle words."}},{"n":3,"text":"पुत्रहन्ता नृशंसोऽहं तव देवि युधिष्ठिरः ।\nशापार्हः पृथिवीनाशे हेतुभूतः शपस्व माम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Goddess, I am Yudhishthira, the cruel killer of your sons, deserving of a curse, the cause of the earth's destruction. Curse me."}},{"n":4,"text":"न हि मे जीवितेनार्थो न राज्येन धनेन वा ।\nतादृशान्सुहृदो हत्वा मूढस्यास्य सुहृद्द्रुहः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have no use for life, nor kingdom, nor wealth, having killed such friends, I who am foolish and a betrayer of friends."}},{"n":5,"text":"तमेवंवादिनं भीतं संनिकर्षगतं तदा ।\nनोवाच किंचिद्गान्धारी निःश्वासपरमा भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he spoke so, frightened and standing near, Gandhari said nothing, sighing deeply."}},{"n":6,"text":"तस्यावनतदेहस्य पादयोर्निपतिष्यतः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्य नृपतेर्धर्मज्ञा धर्मदर्शिनी ।\nअङ्गुल्यग्राणि ददृशे देवी पट्टान्तरेण सा ॥","meaning":{"en":"As King Yudhishthira bowed his body to fall at her feet, the goddess, who knew and saw dharma, saw the tips of his toes through the edge of her blindfold."}},{"n":7,"text":"ततः स कुनखीभूतो दर्शनीयनखो नृपः ।\nतं दृष्ट्वा चार्जुनोऽगच्छद्वासुदेवस्य पृष्ठतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that king whose nails had been beautiful became ugly-nailed. Seeing this, Arjuna went behind Vasudeva."}},{"n":8,"text":"एवं संचेष्टमानांस्तानितश्चेतश्च भारत ।\nगान्धारी विगतक्रोधा सान्त्वयामास मातृवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them moving about here and there like this, descendant of Bharata, Gandhari, her anger gone, comforted them like a mother."}},{"n":9,"text":"तया ते समनुज्ञाता मातरं वीरमातरम् ।\nअभ्यगच्छन्त सहिताः पृथां पृथुलवक्षसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With her leave, the broad-chested Pandavas went together to their mother Pritha, the mother of heroes."}},{"n":10,"text":"चिरस्य दृष्ट्वा पुत्रान्सा पुत्राधिभिरभिप्लुता ।\nबाष्पमाहारयद्देवी वस्त्रेणावृत्य वै मुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing her sons after a long time, overwhelmed with grief for her sons, the goddess shed tears, covering her face with her garment."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो बाष्पं समुत्सृज्य सह पुत्रैस्तथा पृथा ।\nअपश्यदेताञ्शस्त्रौघैर्बहुधा परिविक्षतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, having shed her tears, Pritha with her sons saw them wounded in many ways by the floods of weapons."}},{"n":12,"text":"सा तानेकैकशः पुत्रान्संस्पृशन्ती पुनः पुनः ।\nअन्वशोचन्त दुःखार्ता द्रौपदीं च हतात्मजाम् ।\nरुदतीमथ पाञ्चालीं ददर्श पतितां भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Touching each of her sons again and again, afflicted with sorrow, she grieved, and she saw Draupadi, her children dead, weeping and fallen on the ground."}},{"text":"द्रौपद्युवाच","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"आर्ये पौत्राः क्व ते सर्वे सौभद्रसहिता गताः ।\nन त्वां तेऽद्याभिगच्छन्ति चिरदृष्टां तपस्विनीम् ।\nकिं नु राज्येन वै कार्यं विहीनायाः सुतैर्मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Noble lady, where are all your grandsons gone, with Subhadra's son? They do not come to you now, though you have not seen them for so long, ascetic lady. What use is a kingdom to me, bereft of my sons?"}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":14,"text":"तां समाश्वासयामास पृथा पृथुललोचना ।\nउत्थाप्य याज्ञसेनीं तु रुदतीं शोककर्शिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Broad-eyed Pritha comforted her, raising the weeping Yajnaseni, who was wasted by grief."}},{"n":15,"text":"तयैव सहिता चापि पुत्रैरनुगता पृथा ।\nअभ्यगच्छत गान्धारीमार्तामार्ततरा स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Together with her, followed by her sons, Pritha herself, more afflicted, went to the afflicted Gandhari."}},{"n":16,"text":"तामुवाचाथ गान्धारी सह वध्वा यशस्विनीम् ।\nमैवं पुत्रीति शोकार्ता पश्य मामपि दुःखिताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gandhari then said to the glorious Draupadi, together with her daughter-in-law Kunti: \"Not so, daughter; do not grieve; look at me too, I am in sorrow."}},{"n":17,"text":"मन्ये लोकविनाशोऽयं कालपर्यायचोदितः ।\nअवश्यभावी संप्राप्तः स्वभावाल्लोमहर्षणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I think this destruction of the world, driven by the turning of Time, was bound to come, and it has come of its own nature, making the hair stand on end."}},{"n":18,"text":"इदं तत्समनुप्राप्तं विदुरस्य वचो महत् ।\nअसिद्धानुनये कृष्णे यदुवाच महामतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It is just this that Vidura's great words foretold, when that wise man spoke to Krishna after the peace attempt failed."}},{"n":19,"text":"तस्मिन्नपरिहार्येऽर्थे व्यतीते च विशेषतः ।\nमा शुचो न हि शोच्यास्ते संग्रामे निधनं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since this matter was unavoidable and is now past, do not grieve. Those who died in battle are not to be pitied."}},{"n":20,"text":"यथैव त्वं तथैवाहं को वा माश्वासयिष्यति ।\nममैव ह्यपराधेन कुलमग्र्यं विनाशितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As you are, so am I. Who will comfort me? By my own fault the foremost family has been destroyed.\""}}]}]}